    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d415">

                <pb facs="0645" n="633" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg633"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 P.W./8–1145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-11">August 11,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received August 11—3:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2263. I have been asked to forward to you the following message: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“His Majesty’s Government have received your communication to the Swiss
                            Government for the <hi rendition="#small-caps">Japanese</hi> Government,
                            and agree.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>The acceptance of the British suggestions in the final text was deeply
                    appreciated here.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
